      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The ASPMN strongly recommends that infants who are being circumcised must receive optimal pain management. \u2018\u2018If a decision for circumcision is made, procedural analgesia should be provided\u2019\u2019 (AAP, 1999, p. 691). Therefore, it is the position of the ASPMN that optimal pain management must be provided throughout the circumcision process. Furthermore, parents must be prepared for the procedure and educated about infant pain assessment. They must also be informed of pharmacologic and integrative pain management therapies that are appropriate before, during, and after the procedure."},
